Decision: initialize all 24 Bash permission and destructive-command regexes once on an explicitly sized 8 MiB standard thread before any provider or permission check.
Reason: the real Bash path compiles 20 safe-command regexes before the four destructive-command regexes observed in the SIGBUS stack; get_or_try_init keeps a transient spawn failure retryable.
Test setup: cold child processes execute a real Bash tool inside the cloud and Ollama loops on a 2 MiB worker. A test-only ShellWork seam is used because macOS forbids creating Tauri's graphical event loop from that worker. The cold regression did not reproduce SIGBUS before the production change on this run, so it is retained as a non-regression test rather than claimed as a red reproduction.
